  "_comment": "Multidimensional structured-scene schema for The Tidal Interval. Setting: Tern Island Marine Research Station, October storm season, present day. Victim: Dr. Sarah Okafor (lead marine biologist). Killer: Piers Dunne (logistics coordinator). Red herring: Dr. Marcus Webb (visiting methodology reviewer). Mechanism: a wooden path marker was moved twelve degrees at the fork of the eastern path two hours before the victim's evening walk — sending her, in storm-darkness, toward an unfenced cliff section rather than the longer safe route. Case-specific dim: TIDAL_TELL — observable environmental/temporal signals (storm intensity, tide stage, generator and radio reliability) that act as the case's structural clock. Each engine turn emits one token per dim.",

